{"id": "EUVD-2026-97686", "enisaUuid": "67cd7199-d8ab-3c82-8632-44a9ace9f783", "description": "FreeRDP before 3.0.0 and 3.6.0 before 3.32.0 renders uninitialized heap memory from un-decoded progressive tiles because the tile->current buffer is allocated without zeroing. A malicious RDP server can send a crafted WBT_TILE_FIRST then WBT_TILE_UPGRADE sequence to paint heap bytes onscreen or abort the client process.", "datePublished": "2026-10-12T16:04:18", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T02:28:09", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:L/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/FreeRDP/FreeRDP/security/advisories/GHSA-4mpr-hmqx-83q8", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/freerdp-before-3.0.0-and-3.6.0-before-3.32.0-uninitialized-heap-disclosure-via-progressive-codec-tile-upgrade"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-109242", "GHSA-wx7m-cfxv-x2x7"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.24, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "d248c27d-0ea4-3a3b-bcd8-c539762f8956", "product": {"name": "FreeRDP", "vendor": {"name": "FreeRDP"}}, "product_version": "0 <3.0.0"}, {"id": "ebe1c056-944f-3c73-b914-e70650911618", "product": {"name": "FreeRDP", "vendor": {"name": "FreeRDP"}}, "product_version": "3.6.0 <3.32.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "6ce79f02-b618-378f-8edf-e9b6f50351f6", "vendor": {"name": "FreeRDP"}}], "isExploited": false}